<section class="ph"><div class="ph-media"><img class="ph-img" src="/assets/img/photos/winter-street.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/winter-street-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/winter-street.webp 1200w" sizes="100vw" width="1200" height="908" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></div><div class="wrap ph-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><i aria-hidden="true">/</i><a href="/mi-cities-served/">Cities</a><i aria-hidden="true">/</i><span aria-current="page">Sterling Heights</span></nav><p class="eyebrow eyebrow-light">Metro Detroit · Macomb County</p><h1>Insurance Appraiser in Sterling Heights, Michigan</h1><p class="ph-lede">Sterling Heights grew fast in the postwar decades, filling with brick ranches and colonials along the Clinton River and Van Dyke Avenue. Today it is one of Michigan’s largest cities, and its basements and roofs drive most of its claims.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-maize" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ic" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-glass" href="/request-claim-review/">Free claim review</a></div><dl class="ph-facts"><div><dt>County</dt><dd>Macomb County</dd></div><div><dt>Region</dt><dd>Metro Detroit</dd></div><div><dt>Inspections</dt><dd>On site</dd></div></dl></div></section>
<div class="wrap layout"><article class="prose">
<div class="local"><div><p class="local-k">Neighborhoods &amp; areas</p><p>Dodge Park area, Clinton River corridor, Van Dyke corridor, Lakeside area, Hall Road corridor, Freedom Hill area</p></div><div><p class="local-k">Housing mix</p><p>Sterling Heights is mostly 1960s–1980s brick ranches, bi-levels and colonials with basements, plus many condominium complexes and some newer construction in the northern part of the city.</p></div><div><p class="local-k">Common claim drivers</p><ul class="chips"><li>Basement flooding</li><li>Sewer backup</li><li>Hail damage</li><li>Wind and fallen trees</li><li>Ice dams</li></ul></div></div>
<h2>Macomb County Claims: An Independent Look at Your Estimate</h2>
<p>Sterling Heights is a city of well-kept brick homes with basements, and many of them have been finished into living space over the years. That raises the stakes when water gets in. It is also a city of condominium complexes, where the association’s policy and each owner’s policy have to work together after a loss.</p>
<h3>Flooding in 2014 and 2021</h3>
<p>The August 11, 2014 storm hit Macomb County hard. Warren, Sterling Heights and neighboring communities saw flooded streets and thousands of flooded basements, and I-696 was underwater. Late June 2021 brought another wave of basement flooding across the Detroit area. Homeowners in neighborhoods near the Clinton River and along the Van Dyke corridor dealt with drain backups and wet basements, and many found that their sewer backup coverage was limited or missing.</p>
<h3>What we look for in a backup estimate</h3>
<p>Insurers sometimes write basement claims as simple cleanup jobs when they are really rebuilds. A thorough estimate should address water category and contamination, extraction and structural drying, removal and replacement of drywall, insulation and flooring, and the furnace, water heater and electrical work that may be needed. Contents, from furniture to stored keepsakes, deserve their own careful inventory. Our <a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/water-sewer-backup-appraisal/">water and sewer backup appraisal</a> service looks at each of these.</p>
<h3>Roofs, hail and wind</h3>
<p>Summer thunderstorms bring hail and straight-line wind to Macomb County most years. The August 24, 2023 storms that produced several tornadoes in southeast Michigan, and the February 2023 ice storm before them, left trees on roofs and fences down across the region. On brick ranches, roofs are often lower-pitched and simpler, but disputes still arise over whether damage is from the storm or from age. An independent inspection with good photo documentation helps settle that.</p>
<p>Many homes in Sterling Heights are now 40 to 60 years old, and that age shows up in claims. Original sump pumps, older electrical panels and aging roofs can all become points of dispute, with insurers sometimes pointing to wear and tear. Clear photos, maintenance records and an independent inspection help separate storm damage from age-related issues when the amount is in question.</p>
<div class="note"><b class="h">Condo owners</b>If you own a condo, read both your HO-6 policy and the association’s master deed and policy. Who covers what after a basement or roof loss depends on those documents.</div>
<p>For a second set of eyes on any estimate, see our <a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/insurance-estimate-second-opinion/">insurance estimate second opinion</a> service, or read <a href="/great-lakes-claim-guides/reading-your-xactimate-estimate/">how to read your Xactimate estimate</a> to spot gaps yourself.</p>
<h2>Services available in Sterling Heights</h2>
<p>Every Michigan Insurance Appraiser service is available to owners in Sterling Heights and surrounding communities, including:</p>
<ul><li><a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/appraisal-demand-representation/">Appraisal Demand Representation</a></li><li><a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/homeowner-claim-appraiser/">Homeowner Claim Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/commercial-condo-hoa-appraisal/">Commercial, Condo &amp; HOA Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/hail-roof-damage-appraisal/">Hail &amp; Roof Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/windstorm-tornado-appraisal/">Windstorm &amp; Tornado Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/ice-dam-frozen-pipe-appraisal/">Ice Dam &amp; Frozen Pipe Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/water-sewer-backup-appraisal/">Water &amp; Sewer Backup Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/fire-smoke-loss-appraisal/">Fire &amp; Smoke Loss Appraisal</a></li></ul>
<h2>Questions from Sterling Heights property owners</h2><div class="qa"><details><summary><span>Do you work with condo associations in Sterling Heights?</span><i class="qa-plus" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><div class="qa-a"><p>Yes. We review estimates and act as appraisers for condo and HOA associations as well as individual unit owners throughout Macomb County.</p></div></details><details><summary><span>My insurer says my roof damage is wear and tear. Can appraisal help?</span><i class="qa-plus" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><div class="qa-a"><p>If the insurer denies that a storm caused any damage, that may be treated as a coverage question. If it accepts some storm damage but disputes how much, appraisal can help settle the amount.</p></div></details></div>
